From: ios-milanf-port (desk phase, 2026-10-25)
Subject: [PATCH] MILANF: Foundation atomic writes swap through HFS exchangedata

Foundation's atomic-write path (used by usermanagerd, among others) asks the
VFS layer for `RENAME_SWAP`: swap two paths on one volume so each name ends up
with the other file's data and attributes, atomically. HFS has no native
RENAME_SWAP, so `kpi_vfs.c` catches `VNOP_RENAMEX` returning `ENOTSUP` with
`flags == VFS_RENAME_SWAP` and falls through to `VNOP_EXCHANGE` instead:

```c
if (_err == ENOTSUP && flags == VFS_RENAME_SWAP && *tvpp != NULLVP &&
    vnode_isreg(*fvpp) && vnode_isreg(*tvpp) &&
    vnode_mount(*fvpp) == vnode_mount(*tvpp)) {
    _err = VNOP_EXCHANGE(*fvpp, *tvpp, 0, ctx);
}
```

That whole arm is wrapped in `#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)`, so on
milanf Foundation's atomic writes hit `ENOTSUP` and fail with
"Failed to atomically swap writing file: Operation not supported" - usermanagerd
logs it every time it tries to atomically replace a preferences file.

Why this is safe to widen for milanf:

* `bsd/conf/files` compiles `bsd/sweet_hfs` (the staged HFS, via
  `xnu/patches/0026-stage-hfs.sh`, which already enumerates `SWEET|MILANF` in
  its board selection, commit `8a9ed6b`). `config/MASTER.arm64.milanf`
  enables `NSWEET_HFS` - without it the MILANF build dies at link on the
  open-source asm/pmap surface, so the flag is definitely on. HFS is present.

* The staged HFS provides `hfs_vnop_exchange` (`bsd/sweet_hfs/core/hfs_vnops.c`,
  wired into the vnode-op table at the `exchange` slot), so `VNOP_EXCHANGE` is
  not an undefined symbol on milanf. The call site's preconditions (two regular
  files, same mount) are generic VFS logic with no board constants.

* Nothing in the arm reads a sweet address, clock, or register. `VNOP_EXCHANGE`,
  `VFS_RENAME_SWAP`, `vnode_isreg` and `vnode_mount` are all board-neutral.

The comment inside the arm says `SWEET:`; once both boards share the gate that
stops being true, so it is reworded board-neutrally. The `#endif` itself is
bare in the source and stays bare - this patch widens one gate and rewords one
comment line, nothing more.

Verified without a compiler: fresh ci-tail (ci-art3 + 0086..0101), the `#if`
gate asserted at exactly 1 occurrence, the comment line asserted at exactly 1
occurrence, CR=0 in source and patch, 0086-0102 sequential apply clean (17/17).
Inventory: 8 sites in 8 files -> **7 in 7**, negated class still 0. Link and
boot unverified; CI in the morning.

diff --git a/bsd/vfs/kpi_vfs.c b/bsd/vfs/kpi_vfs.c
index 90cd9fc..8c2b60c 100644
--- a/bsd/vfs/kpi_vfs.c
+++ b/bsd/vfs/kpi_vfs.c
@@ -4459,9 +4459,9 @@ vn_rename(struct vnode *fdvp, struct vnode **fvpp, struct componentname *fcnp, s
 					_err = VNOP_RENAME(fdvp, *fvpp, fcnp, tdvp, *tvpp, tcnp, ctx);
 				}
 			}
-#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
+#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET) || defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_MILANF)
